  "body": "## Complete smooth classification with credited prior obstruction\n\nFor every n >= 1, exactly the all-real-spectrum Segre/Jordan types occur on a\nnonempty open subset of R^n for a smooth compactly supported real Nijenhuis\n(1,1)-tensor. The construction permits arbitrary prescribed numerical real\neigenvalues, multiplicities, equality patterns and Jordan block sizes. Type\nchanges away from the realization domain are allowed.\n\nThe full analytic proof includes the torus-collar torsion identity, finite\nordered arrow deletion and scalar drift for every Jordan block, smooth\nendpoint plateaus, same-dimensional torus embedding and exact zero extension.\nThe independent written audit and acceptance accompany the proof. Aggregate\nfinite checks are supporting metadata; no computational extrapolation or\nomitted executable is a premise of the general theorem.\n\nNecessity is credited to Bolsinov\u2013Konyaev\u2013Matveev, Nijenhuis Geometry,\nTheorem 6.1: https://arxiv.org/abs/1903.04603v2 . The real semisimple and\ntwo-dimensional Jordan cases were already credited by the original problem\nsource. The exact primary locator is Problem 5.11, PDF page 29, in\nhttps://arxiv.org/abs/1804.03737v2 ; the earlier v1 is Problem 4.10, PDF page 37.\nThe corpus label 5.9 is not substituted for either primary locator.\n\n## Distribution and review limits\n\nExactly eight authored proof/audit/acceptance/status and public-source-review\nor metadata files are added under `unsolved_math_prioritization/attempts/2100509/`.\nAll mathematical statements, arguments, examples and qualifications are\npreserved. Editorial changes remove private workflow/revision provenance,\nreplace unavailable script references with permitted aggregate metadata,\nstate review limits and bind the public proof and audit exactly.\n\nThis AI-assisted, unrefereed edition claims no bibliographic priority,\nexhaustive preexisting-current-openness certificate, external human peer\nreview, journal acceptance or formal proof-assistant certification. Programs,\nraw generated outputs, datasets, copied third-party source bodies or images,\nand private coordination material are excluded. Recorded scholarly inspection\nhistory is not a new retrieval, source rehash, inspection or literature search\nby edition preparation.\n\nQUEUE.md and unrelated entries remain unchanged. Editorial preparation adds\nno substantive proof turn and resets no historical accounting. No merge,\nrelease, DOI or outside outreach is requested.\n\nBase commit: `f6caddda8f8be2cdb3e91494325d8f7f365bc3fc`.\n\n## Exact distributed file identities\n\n- `ACCEPTANCE.json`: 1,661 bytes; SHA-256 `3fd00339eafc3793e9a433a72d6aca969b284bc1ce4bb902e288ee316e238ce0`.\n- `MANIFEST.json`: 1,608 bytes; SHA-256 `027426bd03416c58be8c3bd768fa57a776c68bc0cb96963ff3beb1bdf5d7fd8d`.\n- `MATHEMATICAL_AUDIT.md`: 15,880 bytes; SHA-256 `ac3f95ee68cf928c7e5862e522aae015d76db3ad84bdf6a06436ffa6be165b8c`.\n- `MATHEMATICAL_REPORT.md`: 10,006 bytes; SHA-256 `b8dda0f0c82f5f0f8bd0c8de608b2a6ddee4e11b4267311ba0ef1d8aedf4486f`.\n- `README.md`: 3,855 bytes; SHA-256 `63431e38fa8c6d0e70e813f440fda14f713d8e08d04fd89ab3ce171fc5b84a9f`.\n- `SOURCE_METADATA.json`: 6,985 bytes; SHA-256 `cd798875c3e1b52850c358115f00b65d4ae0643257ada45739b0985853ff1ab5`.\n- `SOURCE_REVIEW.md`: 4,603 bytes; SHA-256 `be9f4dabf8f0f4ddaa8fbeab429ebcbe439565037183a3c9c5a11f458ee00b1a`.\n- `STATUS.json`: 1,296 bytes; SHA-256 `32ebda8f9707d0d32f1145d80827b0423204dd85cb320aae2a0e57a3e5b4a880`.\n\nThe manifest lists eight members and hashes the other seven; this body pins the manifest independently.\n",
